<title>MONGOLIA: Mongolia copper production up 22 pct in Jan-May.</title>
<headline>Mongolia copper production up 22 pct in Jan-May.</headline>
<dateline>ULAN BATOR 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mongolian copper concentrate production increased 22 percent to 185,800 tonnes in January-May, compared with 152,300 tonnes in the year-ago period, official state statistics available on Wednesday said.</p>
<p>However, exports of copper concentrate in the first five months of this year fell 9.3 percent to 177,400 tonnes, compared with 195,600 tonnes in the year-ago period, the State Statistical Bulletin said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
</text>
